thread:
maya: Hey team — onboarding sample app hit a weird one. We call /embeddings with a batch of 3, one request times out and the SDK retry sends the single item again but the batching helper re-orders indexes. End result: rerank payloads get mismatched vectors.

sam: ugh. do you have the raw request/response? which SDK (node/python) and which helper?

maya: Node SDK, using the embedBatch helper from sample-app. Quick paste of what I see in logs:

```json
{"batch_id":"b-123","items":[{"id":"a","text":"x"},{"id":"b","text":"y"},{"id":"c","text":"z"}]}
```

Then after a timeout on item b we get a retry flow that looks like:

```json
{"retry_for":"b","items":[{"id":"b","text":"y"}]}
```

But the helper merges responses by array position, not id, so final vector list becomes [vec_a, vec_c, vec_b] while consumer expects [a,b,c].

todd: That sounds like an idempotency/order bug. Helper should re-merge by id, or preserve original ordering using an index map.

sasha: Also check if the SDK's retry attaches an idempotency key for the single-item retry. If the server dedups, it might return the original position but the helper still reindexes.

maya: No idempotency key right now. Sample-app code is simple: it slices batch and calls client.embed(items). The client returns arrays which the helper then flattens. I can paste the helper logic if useful.

sam: Please paste. Small code smells usually. We intentionally try to keep helper minimal but it must account for partial failures.

maya: snippet from embed-helper.js:

```js
async function embedBatch(items){
  const chunks = chunk(items, 3);
  const out = [];
  for(const c of chunks){
    try{
      const resp = await client.embeddings.create({input:c.map(x=>x.text)});
      out.push(...resp.data);
    }catch(e){
      // naive retry single items
      for(const it of c){
        const r = await client.embeddings.create({input:[it.text]});
        out.push(r.data[0]);
      }
    }
  }
  return out; // <-- preserves arrival order, not input order
}
```

maya: So bug is obvious: return array order depends on successful chunk vs item retry ordering. Need to reassemble by original ids.

todd: fix: change helper to attach original index and id in each request, then on response map back. Something like: send [{id, idx, text}] and client returns vectors with ids. If server doesn't echo id, helper should keep a local map of idx->id and put results back into an output array at their original positions.

sasha: Agree. Also this ties into SDK parity: our Python helper already provides a map-based reassembly for partial retries (Iirc @sam implemented that last quarter). Node helper lagging. We should sync implementations.

sam: Yep. Node helper was kept minimal. I'll open a PR to: 1) include original index in the request envelope, 2) on retries preserve mapping, and 3) add an option to enable idempotency-key header per-item.

maya: Thanks. One more UX note: the rerank sample expects consumer to pair vectors by array index; we should document that helpers guarantee input-order in their readme (and not rely on server echo). Could also add a test in sample-app verifying that after a simulated partial failure the order remains consistent.

ci-bot: ci/test-embed-helper: unit tests for embed-helper reassembly added (w/ simulated timeouts) — triggered by @sam patch.

sam: I'll also add an integration test that uses the rerank path: produce vectors in shuffled arrival order and assert final ordering equals input id order.

maya: One last thing — response format: some teams expect the embeddings envelope to be {id, embedding} but our embedded responses from hosted API are position-only arrays. We should surface both patterns in the SDK so sample apps don't invent fragile parsers.

todd: Good call. We can add an optional param `return_items: true` to client.embeddings.create that asks server to echo ids when present. For now, helper-level mapping is the safest.

sasha: To sum up: immediate fix is helper change + test. Medium: Node/Python parity pass. Long: spec update on embedding response envelope and doc note for rerank sample.

maya: Perfect. I'll patch the sample-app helper today and leave a note in onboarding docs. Thanks! :thumbsup:
